meta {
  name: Update Pay Statement Inputs
  type: http
  seq: 48
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/payouts/statements/{{payoutsStatementId}}/inputs
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{payoutsOwnerToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "compliancePercent": 97,
    "retentionPercent": null,
    "lifeReferrals": null,
    "meetingAttendance": null
  }
}

script:pre-request {
  if (!bru.getVar("payoutsStatementId")) bru.runner.skipRequest();
}

script:post-response {
  // Net pay before any entered adjustments: Update Pay Statement Adjustments
  // checks its amounts against it.
  if (res.getStatus() === 200) {
    bru.setVar("payoutsNetPay", res.getBody().totals.netPay);
  }
}

tests {
  test("returns 200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("stores the figures whole and says which the structure reads", function () {
    const body = res.getBody();
    expect(body.id).to.equal(bru.getVar("payoutsStatementId"));
    expect(body.inputs).to.eql({
      compliancePercent: 97,
      retentionPercent: null,
      lifeReferrals: null,
      meetingAttendance: null,
    });
    expect(body.inputsNeeded).to.have.keys(
      "compliance",
      "retention",
      "referrals",
      "attendance",
    );
    expect(body.indicators.compliancePercent).to.equal(97);
  });

  test("totals carry net pay", function () {
    const totals = res.getBody().totals;
    expect(totals.netPay).to.be.a("number");
    expect(totals.basePay).to.be.a("number");
  });
}

docs {
  # PATCH /payouts/statements/:id/inputs — the figures the manager enters (2026 comp plans)

  **Module** — `payouts`. **Permission** — `payouts:write`, within your data
  scope (a statement outside it is a `404`). Not on your **own** statement
  unless you also hold `agency:payouts:admin` — the figures decide your pay.

  The 2026 pay plans depend on figures the app does not hold. The manager
  enters them on each draft; `null` = not entered. A gate that needs a figure
  is **not met** until it is entered; a penalty applies only to an entered one.

  | Field | Read by |
  |---|---|
  | `compliancePercent` (0–100) | the compliance floor (below it: no Sales of the Month, hat trick, team or tier bonuses, base rates, a % off variable pay), compliance-gated rate steps and tiers, Producer of the Year |
  | `retentionPercent` (0–100) | rate steps measured on retention (Client Relations Manager) |
  | `lifeReferrals` (whole, 0–1000) | the referral rule (shortfall deduction / bonus) |
  | `meetingAttendance` (boolean) | the team bonus's attendance requirement |

  The body is all four, whole. The statement is then recalculated exactly as
  **Recalculate Pay Statement** does — against the month's stored team split
  and Salesperson of the Month. When the figures change who shares the pool
  or can win the month, the warnings say to recalculate the month (**Generate
  Payout Run**), which keeps every statement's figures.

  `inputsNeeded` on the response says which figures this statement's
  structure reads, so the page asks only for those.

  **Response `200`** — the statement, as **Get Pay Statement**.

  **Errors** — `400` a figure out of range; `403` without `payouts:write`, or
  `PAYOUT_STATEMENT_OWN_INPUTS` on your own statement; `404` outside your
  scope; `409` `PAYOUT_STATEMENT_NOT_EDITABLE` once sent or accepted,
  `PAYOUT_STATEMENT_CHANGED` when it changed meanwhile: the figures and the
  statement recalculated from them are one write, onto the statement as it
  was read (PAC-182 review).
}
